== Policies
. Attendance and completion of readings before each class are expected.
. Late work is handled individually; please reach out before the deadline.
. We follow the [https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/studentaffairs/sccs/conduct.php Code of Student Responsibility]; additional expectations will be discussed and established together in the first class.
. We follow the University's [https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/academic_integrity/policies_procedures/index.php Academic Integrity Policy] (including on [https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/academic_integrity/generative-ai/index.php?accordion=content-d19e272 Generative AI and LLMs]); any use must be disclosed. Faculty are required to report suspected violations to the Academic Judiciary.
. If a disability may affect your coursework, contact the [mailto:sasc@stonybrook.edu Student Accessibility Support Center] (Stony Brook Union Suite 107, 631-632-6748) to arrange accommodations. All information is confidential.
. Course materials posted online are for the exclusive use of students enrolled in this course and may not be redistributed, per the TEACH Act.
. Disruptive behavior that compromises the learning environment may be reported to the Office of University Community Standards.

